RF.put("questb:b8",{"7368":{"id":7368,"t":"Defusing the Threat","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Find the Stormpike Explosives Expert and kill him. Return to the Frostwolf Explosives Expert when the task is complete.\nStormpike Explosives Expert slain","desc":"I know all about landmines. I'm the one that lays all the mines on the front lines here, after all.\nIf you want to defuse the Stormpike mine fields, all you have to do is kill their explosives expert. That dwarven coward is no doubt hiding in the first tower on the Field of Strife. Take him out and those landmines won't come back after they've been disarmed.\nIf you do happen to kill him, come back here and let me know. No good deed should go unrewarded.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\nLevel 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7368","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8168":{"id":8168,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the farm, then return to Field Marshal Oslight in Refuge Pointe.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nFarm Assaulted","desc":"‹name›, the battle for Arathi Basin is a battle for resources and territory. Key points in the area must be held and operated in order to supply our forces with much needed raw materials and supplies. I charge you to assault the points farthest from our Arathi Basin base.\nAssault the farm, the mine, the lumber mill and the blacksmith when they are controlled by the enemy. Find the enemy's banner and rip it from its flag post!\nWhen you have done this to all four points, return to me.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Field Marshal Oslight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"728":{"id":728,"t":"To the Undercity for Yagyin's Digest","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Sigil of the Hammer to Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity.\nSigil of the Hammer\nProvided: Sigil of the Hammer","desc":"The tablet tells much. But not enough! Not nearly enough!\nThere is a book, a digest that Yagyin wrote in ages past. The... people I fled from... they keep this book in many places. And their most learned study it. It holds vast knowledge. Knowledge to protect us!\nGo to Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity of Lordaeron. Show him this sigil and he'll think you one of them. Ask him for Yagin's Digest...and bring it to me!","rew":"Experience: 775","back":"Ah, we have an eager ‹class›, I see. Are you here to learn from my collection? Good!\nBut be warned: just as knowledge gives power to the strong...it will drive the weak mad.","done":"Be discrete with your signs, ‹class›. There are those who do not believe the righteousness of our pledge.\nAnd there are those who would see us fail if they knew of us.\nWe must always be careful. And watchful. And patient.\nBadlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":51.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Theldurin the Lost","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":53.7,"y":54.5,"n":"Keeper Bel'dugur","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4808":{"id":4808,"t":"Felnok Steelspring","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Tinkee's Letter to Felnok Steelspring.\nTinkee's Letter\nProvided: Tinkee's Letter","desc":"I have another favor to ask of you.\nMy initial study of the essence you collected shows that it might be possible to freeze dragon whelp eggs and preserve them! I want to test this theory, but first I need specially made engineering components. My colleague, Felnok Steelspring, can make them.\nHere, take this letter to Felnok. It tells him what I need. You'll find Felnok in Winterspring, in the town of Everlook.","rew":"Experience: 2,700\n+50 reputation with Everlook","back":"It's cold up here! I hope you brought me a blanket!","done":"That's no blanket! But what have we here? I letter from Tinkee? I wonder what she has to say...\nAh, she's studying in the Burning Steppes. That makes sense--that's a good source for dragonkin. Oh, but look! It says here that she needs some parts for a device she wants to build. I guess that's where I come in, eh?\nBurning Steppes Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":24,"n":"Tinkee Steamboil","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.6,"y":38.6,"n":"Felnok Steelspring","e":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97928":{"id":97928,"t":"Camping 101 blacksmithing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Thrag Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your blacksmithing skill to 20","desc":"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39.2,"y":56.2,"n":"Thrag Stonehoof","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94248":{"id":94248,"t":"Craftsmans writ blue overalls","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Blue Overalls\nBlue Overalls","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Blue Overalls, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Oh! Please keep your voice down--we don't need to draw any further attention to ourselves.\nDo you have something for me?","done":"The Blue Overalls! Thank goodness, I have a proper change of clothes.\nTake this, and please be on your way. I do not have time to chat, I must keep an eye on the farm and can't risk more distractions.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":34,"y":23.3,"n":"Alyce","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94328":{"id":94328,"t":"Craftsmans writ mithril spurs","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Mithril Spurs\nMithril Spurs","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Mithril Spurs, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Mithril Spurs Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94328","cats":["crafting"]},"7928":{"id":7928,"t":"Darkmoon Warlords Deck","lv":55,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Warlords Deck to the Darkmoon Faire when it comes to town.\nWarlords Deck","desc":"Now that you have gathered all of the Warlord cards together into a deck, a ninth card mysteriously appears with the same backing as the first eight. On this card is inscribed, \"Return these cards to the Darkmoon Faire and be rewarded.\" You have heard that this faire alternately stops at Mulgore and Goldshire every few months, so you will have to wait until they are here next.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Card: Heroism\nExperience: 550\n+150 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"I see that you have managed to complete a deck of warlords! Congratulations!","done":"So you have put together a deck of Warlords. Your gesture of returning it to us will create a tie between you and the Darkmoon that will not soon be forgotten. Allow me to present you with one of the greater darkmoon cards as a small token of our appreciation.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.4,"y":45,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.3,"y":70.1,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"4728":{"id":4728,"t":"Beached Sea Creature","lv":14,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Creature Bones Beached Sea Creature\nProvided: Sea Creature Bones","desc":"The corpse of what appears to be some sort of giant sea mammal lies partially gutted on the beach. A wheelbarrow and various tools lie abandoned by this enormous beached sea creature, as though an attempt to study it had been made previously. Though murlocs have scavenged this beast, enough of it remains to gather a suitable sample for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! What brings you back to Auberdine? Are you here to report on another discovery, perhaps?","done":"Ah, I believe you discovered one that was originally being examined by the Explorer's League. They have a presence here in Darkshore, and they had mentioned that they were studying one of the beached creatures until they were chased out by the murlocs. You appear to have succeeded where we both have not. Please - accept this honorarium on behalf of the Temple of the Moon.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36,"y":70.9,"n":"Beached Sea Creature","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"968":{"id":968,"t":"The Powers Below","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Book: The Powers Below to Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern, Ironforge.\nBook: The Powers Below Twilight Thug 5 % , Twilight Disciple 5 %\nProvided: Book: The Powers Below","desc":"Although terribly worn and scratched, the title of this book can still be read upon its cover:\nThe Powers Below\nInside the book is a listing of unpronounceable names with foreboding titles, methods of worship, and preferred sacrifices...many of which include living, humanoid creatures.\nOn the inside cover of the book are the words: \"Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms, The Forlorn Cavern, Ironforge. Proprietor: Gerrig Bonegrip.\"\nIf Bonegrip sells books like this, perhaps he'll buy this one back.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello, sir/madam.\nMay I interest you in one of my tomes?","done":"Ah, a copy of The Powers Below. An interesting text, this is. And some might find it useful...\nBut this one's in sad shape. And look here! There are notes in the margin of almost every page!\nHm...I know this copy. I sold it to Bolgar last year. Are you...a friend of his? Yes, I thought you were. You have that same fire behind your eyes!\nWell, by definition, a friend of Bolgar's is a friend of mine. And we take care of our own, yes?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Gerrig Bonegrip","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98888":{"id":98888,"t":"Conflict at darkspear islands","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Level 39\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor\nThe Barrens Alterac Mountains Arathi Highlands Undercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.6,"y":8.6,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":63,"y":59.8,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.6,"y":29.2,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.2,"y":97.6,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.4,"y":30.4,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":57.8,"y":76.8,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1368":{"id":1368,"t":"Gelkis Alliance","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nReach 3000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"To beat the centaur, we must use their hatred against them. We will ally with one of the clans and through them, we will learn how to defeat all the clans.\nIf you choose to ally with the Gelkis then slay their most hated rival, the Magram. After you earn the respect of the Gelkis, meet with the Gelkis shaman Uthek the Wise, on the outskirts of the Gelkis Village, in southwest Desolace.","rew":"Experience: 650\n-500 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n+100 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","back":"Your two feet step on Gelkis earth. You are not welcome here!\nProve you seek friendship with the Gelkis. Kill Magram centaur. Return when the ground is wet with Magram blood.","done":"The earth speaks to me. And it says you have killed many Magram. This is good.\nIf you are a friend of the Gelkis, then listen. I have more tasks for you.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":56.3,"y":59.7,"n":"Gurda Wildmane","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":36.2,"y":79.2,"n":"Uthek the Wise","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"93128":{"id":93128,"t":"Khan jehn","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and slay Khan Jhen at Magram Village. Once you have succeeded, report to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nKhan Jehn slain\nGelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"As much as I would like Uthek or Khan Shaka to give the order, I fear our window of opportunity is short. Too short to consult those at Gelkis Village.\nI believe with the situation unfolding here at the Valley of Bones that the Magram have left Khan Jehn with minimal defenses. If there was ever a time to attack another clan's Khan, it is now.\nBut ‹name›, a Khan is not to be trifled with, least of all Jehn. If you are brave enough to make your move, you must be swift but do not underestimate him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAbandoned Ferocity Thrice-Damned Effigy Bludgeon of Betrayed Virtues\nExperience: 3,450\n+6,000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\nDesolace Open the zone on the world map Level 42 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 38 40 45 53 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93128\nThe chain\n4 quests from level 42 to 43, 9,810 XP in all.\n1 [ 42 ] Saving Our Own\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis clan, and rescue 5 Gelkis Captives within the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n[ 42 ] Bone Burying\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and dispel the curses from 8 failed summons throughout the Valley of Bones.\n3,450 XP\n2 [ 43 ] Checking Things Out\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and investigate centaur points of interest within Shen'dralas.\n360 XP\n3 [ 42 ] Khan Jehn this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and slay Khan Jhen at Magram Village.\n3,450 XP","cats":["desolace"]},"6568":{"id":6568,"t":"The Testament of Rexxar","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Rexxar's Letter to Myranda the Hag in the Western Plaguelands.\nRexxar's Testament\nProvided: Rexxar's Testament","desc":"Illusion and disguise. That is how you will fool the Black Dragonflight, and gain what you seek.\nThough I could teach you something of the skills of deception, you need the help of a master.\nI know of one who could do this. In the Western Plaguelands, you will find Myranda the Hag, once a master illusionist of Lordaeron. She has helped us in the past, and if she believes the cause worthy, she may help you.\nTake this message to her.","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"It is not often I see one of the Horde in these parts of Lordaeron. What is it that you have for Myranda?","done":"<Myranda holds the note, pauses, then smiles.>\nHow is he? Rexxar, I mean. Oh, come now, do not look so confused. The letter was left intentionally blank. It carried with it the intentions and thoughts of its creator. Judging from its contents, it is no wonder Rexxar left it as such. Imagine if you were captured or slain and this information discovered!\nOh, nevermind! Myranda will help you, ‹race›. I owe the Warchief a favor or two.\n<Myranda smiles.>\nFeralas Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":46.4,"y":18.2,"n":"Rexxar","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":50.8,"y":77.8,"n":"Myranda the Hag","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5528":{"id":5528,"t":"The Gordok Taste Test","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 56 instead of 57.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Gordok Green Grog 5 Kreeg's Stout Beatdown","done":"You da big boss now, so you get free sample of my better brews! These drinks boost you up AND give you good buzz! These are da good ones, chief... you try and tell Kreeg yourself!\nStart Stomper Kreeg End Stomper Kreeg Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 5528","cats":["dire-maul"]},"5928":{"id":5928,"t":"Heeding the Call","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nIt has come to my attention that Turak Runetotem has put out word that he wishes to speak with you. It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally. Turak is one of the Arch Druid's assistants; he is known as a wise and patient druid, and he should teach you well.\nHe is located in Thunder Bluff, inside the Cenarion Circle's main tent on the Elder Rise.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am glad you found your way here today. young ‹class›. The time has come for you to take a large step into a much larger world.\nInside each of Cenarius' children is the call to serve nature. Animals and plants are our friends as well as our charges. We choose to devote our lives as preservers of balance for their sakes as well as our own. Your first step into this world will be to learn of the ways of the bear, and to learn strength of body and heart.\nReady yourself!","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":45.8,"y":64.7,"n":"Innkeeper Pala","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"96408":{"id":96408,"t":"A visitor to dun morogh","lv":13,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Investigate the campsite overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.","desc":"Last night one of our mountaineers spotted a campfire on a hillside to the east. It looks to be pretty high up, overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.\nIt's probably nothing, but I'd like you to go check on that camp. If they are friendly, no harm done. If they aren't friendly... well, you know what to do.","done":"Greetings, friend. How are ya?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":50.4,"y":49,"n":"Beldin Steelgrill","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":64.8,"y":58.4,"n":"Earthseer Farsen","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"808":{"id":808,"t":"Minshina's Skull","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Minshina's skull from the circle of power on the Echo Isles.\nBring it to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.\nMinshina's Skull Imprisoned Darkspear","desc":"I hear the voice of my brother, Minshina, calling to me in my dreams.\nHe was taken by Zalazane, the warlock on the Echo Isles to the east. And he is dead.\nBut death is not freedom for my brother. Minshina's spirit was trapped within his own skull by Zalazane's magics. In my dreams I see it with other skulls, in a circle of power on the largest Echo Isle. As long as it remains there my brother's soul is doomed.\nPlease, ‹name›. Find the circle and retrieve Minshina's skull. Bring it to me.\nFree him!","rew":"You will receive:\nFaintly Glowing Skull\nExperience: 775\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Do you have my brother's skull, ‹name›? Is he finally free?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. You have saved Minshina. You have saved my brother's spirit from slavery!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.7,"n":"Master Gadrin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"99048":{"id":99048,"t":"A missing hand","lv":11,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Heglan Shadeeye north of Tiragarde Keep.","desc":"A member of the Shattered Hand, a group of more... subtle fighters, was watching Tiragarde Keep from a distance. Her reports suddenly stopped coming in.\nI doubt the humans would have caught her, so I'm concerned something more dangerous is at play. See if you can find her. Hopefully the messages are just delayed.","done":"Heglan's body lies cold within the wreckage of the hut.\nWhatever killed her doesn't seem to be human. There may be signs of what happened nearby.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Orgnil Soulscar","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":58.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Heglan Shadeeye","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1288":{"id":1288,"t":"Vimess report","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Vimes's Report to Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore.\nProvided: Vimes's Report","desc":"You've done some good work, ‹name›, best I've seen from an amateur.\nLady Proudmoore asked that I keep her apprised of this delicate situation, and I haven't spoken to her for some time now.\nI was going to deliver my report to her later, but it seems more fitting that you should be the one to speak with her about it. You can probably answer her questions better than I could.\nLevel 38 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 34 36 41 48 Side Both factions Quest ID 1288","cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9128":{"id":9128,"t":"The Elemental Equation","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Core of Elements.\n30 Core of Elements Huricanian 95.7 % , Smoldar 91.6 % , The Windreaver 79.8 % , Dust Stormer 79.3 % and 4 more","desc":"Greetings, adventurer! Are you interested in some work? I pay those under my employ with insignias. These insignias can be used at the Quartermaster to purchase items of power.\nAll I need you to do is bring me as many core of elements as you can carry. The more the better!\nYou'll find them on elementals of varying shapes and sizes that exist across our world.","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Dawn\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"I can only steer you in the right direction, ‹name›.","done":"A job well done, ‹name›! As promised, the INsignia is yours. Just remember, there's more WHERE that came from...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"99128":{"id":99128,"t":"Slimy menace","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill the murlocs at Crystal Lake.\nMurloc Streamrunner slain : 0/ 4\nMurloc slain : 0/ 7","desc":"This can only be the work of those murlocs on the other side of the lake. They're disgusting little things, with a vicious temper and teeth to match.\nIf we let this continue, there won't be any fish to speak of anywhere in this lake. If you could clear them out a bit, it would help me a ton.","back":"Are they dead?","done":"I can hear their warbling from here, it'll be in my nightmares. Well, that should slow them down--although I have no doubt that they'll make up those numbers quickly.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.4,"y":62.2,"n":"Jason Mathers","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"88":{"id":88,"t":"Princess Must Die!","lv":9,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Princess, grab her collar, then bring it back to Ma Stonefield at the Stonefield Farm.\nBrass Collar Princess","desc":"The Brackwells have a prize-winning pig, Princess. The sow is HUGE, and she got that way from sneaking over here and eating my veggies!\nSo before she comes to our fields...Princess must die! Bring me her collar as proof of the deed and I'll give you something for your time!\nPrincess is usually over at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, to the east and beyond the Maclure farm. Get her before she gets hungry and comes back here!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWeather-worn Boots Brass-studded Bracers Farmer's Boots\nExperience: 775\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you see her yet? Did you get her?","done":"Thank goodness! That pig was getting so big she'd have eaten our whole crop! Thank you, ‹name›.\nNow, do either of these suit you?","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":34.7,"y":84.5,"n":"Ma Stonefield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3128":{"id":3128,"t":"Natural Materials","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Splintered Logs, 6 Encrusted Minerals, 20 pieces of Resilient Sinew, and 40 Metallic Fragments to Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Camp Mojache.\n2 Splintered Log Wandering Forest Walker 80 %\n6 Encrusted Minerals Zapped Cliff Giant 80 % , Zapped Land Walker 80 % , Cliff Giant 80 % , Land Walker 80 % and 3 more\n20 Resilient Sinew Antilus the Soarer 80 % , Marauding Owlbeast 80 % , Frayfeather Hippogryph 80 % , Frayfeather Stagwing 80 % and 4 more\n40 Metallic Fragments Zapped Cliff Giant 80 % , Zapped Land Walker 80 % , Antilus the Soarer 80 % , Marauding Owlbeast 80 % and 4 more","desc":"I will need certain materials to complete my endeavor... You may do this alongside the other tasks I will give you.\nI'll need a splintered log from a treant of Feralas. Encrusted minerals, these can be found on the mountain giants and faerie dragons to the west. Also, find me some resilient sinew from the owlbeasts of the Hinterlands or hippogryphs of Feralas. Finally, I'll need a large amount of metallic fragments from any of these creatures I mentioned.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Were you able to collect the materials I need?","done":"Excellent! These materials, combined with the muisek, should yield just the results we've been wanting.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"6088":{"id":6088,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Swoop. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"The final task that I have for you requires that you tame a creature that inhabits the sky. The swoop is a difficult opponent, but as your ally, you will acquire its sharp attacks and threatening presence.\nBy the will of the Earthmother, when you return I will bestow you with the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing to be your companion; this creature will face the challenges you face, and gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as you wish.","rew":"You will learn: Taming Lesson\nExperience: 850","back":"You will soon be ready, ‹name›.","done":"You have learned all I can teach you, ‹name›. May the blessings of the Earthmother guide you in choosing a pet.\nHere you are, ‹name›. I will now give you the power to tame a beast, as well as call it and dismiss it as you see fit. Use your new skills with pride and honor the Earthmother.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"3448":{"id":3448,"t":"Passing the Burden","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tymor in Ironforge.","desc":"I've recently been handed the responsibility of investigating Azshara--a once beautiful area the elves called home. This would be back when they practiced magic. It's now a more dangerous place than it is beautiful, but that doesn't stop us from turning over every stone for answers to our past.\nA companion of mine named Tymor offered to help me investigate the area since he takes a particular interest in such things.\nHe owns a small place to the right of the Hall of Mysteries here in the city.","rew":"Experience: 500","done":"Ah, Karnik sent you, did he? I expected to hear from him soon. I've discovered such wonderful things about Azshara.. I know night elves have incredible life spans, but everyone forgets some of the more... unfortunate events in their lives sometimes. That's not meant as a criticism, just an observation.\nLong ago, there were cities created by the elves filled with knowledge about magic and other lost arts. Being a student of such things, I started my investigation. What I found was quite thrilling.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.1,"y":21.9,"n":"Tymor","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8648":{"id":8648,"t":"Darkcore the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":62,"y":73.2,"n":"Elder Darkcore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9368":{"id":9368,"t":"The Festival of Fire","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Touch the bonfires within Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, and the Undercity, then speak to a Festival Talespinner within the capital cities.\nFlame of Orgrimmar used\nFlame of Thunder Bluff used\nFlame of the Undercity used","desc":"Midsummer is upon us once again!\nEach year, as tradition dictates, Flamekeepers are chosen to tend the bonfires within our capitals. While fires are burning throughout Azeroth, it is imperative that ours be the hottest and brightest, to properly pay homage to the season.\nIn fact, I have a task for you, if you don't mind. I've not yet heard if the fires in all capitals are properly burning. Travel there yourself and warm yourself by the fires--make sure they're hot!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Burning Blossom 10 Fiery Festival Brew\nExperience: 650","back":"Have you had any luck, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. With the shadows destroyed, it can only be a matter of time before the Lich King decides to recall his necropolises and leave us in peace.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":21.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.8,"y":34.9,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":73.1,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"7848":{"id":7848,"t":"Attunement to the Core","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to the Molten Core entry portal in Blackrock Depths and recover a Core Fragment. Return to Lothos Riftwaker in Blackrock Mountain when you have recovered the Core Fragment.\nCore Fragment Core Fragment","desc":"Rifts stir, tear, and collapse all around us, ‹race›. Not two paces from where I stand is a tear leading through the depths of Blackrock Mountain, into the maw of the Firelord.\nSurprised? Pity... The mortal races cannot comprehend that which they cannot see, touch, or feel.\nI assure you, the portal is there and access is possible.\nI've piqued your interest? Attunement is simple. Venture into Blackrock Depths and retrieve a core fragment. Return it to me and I shall attune your essence with the portal.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"You must attune your soul with the Molten Core before access is granted.","done":"I am now able to transport you to the Molten Core. Ask and it shall be done.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":26.4,"y":24.5,"n":"Lothos Riftwaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["molten-core"]},"9048":{"id":9048,"t":"Redemption Handguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Redemption Handguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Handguards, 8 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Handguards\n8 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Handguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Redemption Handguards.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"91208":{"id":91208,"t":"Coming to terms","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Frightened Paladin in Deathknell.\nOffer aid to the Frightened Paladin","desc":"Not all of our fellow Paladins who rise again are quick to acclimate to our new reality. Some struggle to reconcile that they are now, in a way, the very thing they spent their lives fighting against.\nThese individuals often simply need a kind gesture and a sympathetic ear. Unfortunately, many others are quick to turn violent. Find the frightened paladin who fled into the hills directly west of this chapel. Extend a hand in friendship. Lead them back into the light if you can.","done":"Tragically, more than a few of our brothers and sisters succumb to a similar madness after being risen. As precious as every Forsaken soul is, sometimes the best we can do is grant those that cannot acclimate a clean end.\nI will say a prayer to the light for her. Thank you for doing what must be done, Keldorn.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31,"y":66.2,"n":"Aramis Hammerhand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"78088":{"id":78088,"t":"A strange artifact","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Althalaxx Orb to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.\nProvided: Althalaxx Orb","desc":"<The mysterious orb you hold fills you with cold dread. You can almost hear a voice echo faintly in your mind. Low and guttural, you understand well that the language being spoken is demonic in nature.\nEven as a paladin, this magic is beyond you. Find a more senior paladin here in Kalimdor who might be able to help you discern the nature of this sinister object.>","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450","back":"Did you find something in the tower?","done":"You were right to bring this to me, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.6,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"248":{"id":248,"t":"Looking Further","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Climb the intact watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep.\nFind a suitable container to place the Glyph of Azora.\nGlyph of Azora\nProvided: Glyph of Azora","desc":"I have been watching the Tower of Ilgalar, and can detect that Morganth is in conflict with the Orcs in Stonewatch Keep. I do not know the reason behind their contention, but you may aid me in unraveling this mystery.\nTake another Glyph of Azora, then go to the top of the intact watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep.\nFind a suitable object on which to place the Glyph. A chest or a jar -- some place where the glyph will not be noticed -- will suit my purpose.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"This jar once held a foul-smelling liquor, but now lies empty and forgotten on a pair of barrels.","done":"It is a suitable vessel for the Glyph of Azora, allowing Theocritus to delve into the minds within Stonewatch Keep.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":79.4,"y":46.8,"n":"Old Lion Statue","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":58.2,"y":49.8,"n":"An Empty Jar","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"98248":{"id":98248,"t":"Shipping label","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Shipping Label to someone at the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade hub near the Crossroads in the Barrens.\nShipping Label","desc":"<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.\n\"Return damaged shipments or empty crates to the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade outpost, now conveniently located due west of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Your time is valuable and we will compensate you for your efforts!\"\nBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>","back":"Good day, traveler. How can I assist?","done":"You found the right place, and you're speaking with the right person! I can jot you down as one of our new associates. No paperwork necessary on your part, I can't be bothered with more of that.\nAll we ask of you is to assist in dealing with compromised deliveries you find out during your travels. Doing so will earn you Merchant's Favor, which you can use to purchase goods and services right here. Here's a bit to get you settled in!\nDo you happen to have the crate this label came with?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":50,"y":29.2,"n":"Dokimi","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"97288":{"id":97288,"t":"Unending Torment","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Deliver the Abominable Head to Master Apothecary Faranell within the Undercity.\nDeliver the Abominable Head to someone within the Undercity.\nProvided: Abominable Head","desc":"<As the creature falls, its head comes toppling off. It seems as if it has been reattached several times, and the connection gets weaker with each reconnection.\nSomeone in the Undercity would know more about this unique abomination.>","back":"What have we here?","done":"Oho! I believe I know this head. A cruel joke by our Dark Lady. A delicious one at that.\nI think I have a use for this.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.4,"y":69.4,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"1048":{"id":1048,"t":"Into The Scarlet Monastery","lv":42,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey and then report back to Varimathras in the Undercity.\nHigh Inquisitor Whitemane slain in Scarlet Monastery\nScarlet Commander Mograine slain in Scarlet Monastery\nHerod slain in Scarlet Monastery\nHoundmaster Loksey slain in Scarlet Monastery","desc":"Whilst the Dark Lady tends to the pressing issue of the Lich King's advance to the north, I am seeing to it that matters closer to home are being taken care of accordingly.\nNo doubt, the human pests who call themselves the Scarlet Crusade are proving to be the sharpest thorn in our side domestically. Tirisfal Glades is literally crawling with the little red ants.\nTravel to the Monastery, ‹class›, and lay waste to High Inquisitor Whitemane and her top lieutenants.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSword of Omen Prophetic Cane Dragon's Blood Necklace\nExperience: 5,150\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"Perhaps I was not explicit in my orders, ‹class›. I want High Inquisitor Whitemane killed once and for all. And while you're at it, take out her top brass as well.\nKill that zealot, Scarlet Commander Mograine. Lay waste to Herod, the Scarlet Champion. And slaughter Houndmaster Loksey and his filthy mutts too.\nNow begone!","done":"You have served the Dark Lady well, ‹class›. 'Twas no small task I asked of you.\nYour loyalty to the Forsaken has been noted. And your tenacity in combat will be remembered.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"3368":{"id":3368,"t":"Suntara Stones","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 1g 40s instead of 1g 30s.","obj":"Take the Singed Letter to Thorius in Ironforge. He is in the Hall of Explorers.\nSinged Letter\nProvided: Singed Letter","desc":"Brother,\nIf you are reading this letter, I am no more. How it got to you, I do not know, but thank and reward the ones responsible.\nAbout the stones: They exist and the Dark Irons have them in their possession. Their leader, Lathoric the Black, is using the power of the stones to enslave my excavation team. They were taken to the cauldron. Their minds are twisted, working night and day to complete something called Obsidion.\nHelp them, brother. It is the final wish of a dead man.\n-Dorius","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"<Thorius sobs.>","done":"<Thorius wipes his face dry.>\nIn the name of the Light, he will have his wish. This I vow.\nSearing Gorge Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":74.4,"y":19.3,"n":"Singed Letter","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Curator Thorius","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"1528":{"id":1528,"t":"Call of Water","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.","desc":"Water be in ya future, mon. I see you be strong in da ways of fire already, an' me tinkin' you be ready to talk to Islen.\nIslen live along the coast of da Barrens. If ya head south along the Southfury River, ya canna miss her--look fer da big shark! She be strong in da ways of da elements and can teach ya da ways of water... if you tink you be ready.\nShe be easy ta find, just don' go too far south--she be jus' beyond Ratchet.","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.\nYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38,"y":37.7,"n":"Searn Firewarder","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8808":{"id":8808,"t":"Uniform Supplies","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Mooncloth, 2 Bolts of Runecloth and 1 Ironweb Spider Silk to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.\nMooncloth\n2 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\nIronweb Spider Silk Mother Smolderweb 50 % , Crystal Fang 47 % , Gretheer 16.2 % , Plague Lurker 13.9 % and 4 more\nLogistics Task Briefing VIII\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing VIII","desc":"The latest influx of volunteers has caused a shortage of uniforms. Procure a batch of uniform materials and bring them to Windcaller Proudhorn.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"1448":{"id":1448,"t":"In Search of The Temple","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind wants you to search for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"There was a time when I was young and full of vigor like you, ‹class›.\nBut now I'm old and unable to explore the world like I once did. Ah, the things I saw!\nBut there was one mystery that eluded me. For my final quest, the Explorers' League sent me in search of The Temple of Atal'Hakkar. It was rumored to be located in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nBecause of my frail state, I traveled the skies by gryphon in search of it but never found it.\nHelp an old dwarf out? Perhaps you will have better luck on foot.","rew":"Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I have traveled the world from the jungles of Azeroth to the snowy peaks of Khaz Modan.\nNever before have I asked for help in my adventures. But my old bones are tired.\nNothing would leave me feeling more satisfied than knowing that I completed my final quest for the Explorers' League\nIf you'd be so kind as to help me search for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, ‹class›, I'd greatly appreciate it.\nScour the Swamp of Sorrows and report back with your findings!","done":"The Temple of Atal'Hakkar has been sunk beneath the Pool of Tears? And surrounded by the green dragonflight?\nAn amazing discovery, ‹class›. But obviously something has gone terribly wrong.\nStormwind City Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69.5,"y":40.4,"n":"Brohann Caskbelly","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"5048":{"id":5048,"t":"Good Natured Emma","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Ol' Emma in Stormwind and see if she is in fact Emma Felstone. If she is, then perhaps she'd like the package Janice Felstone made for her.\nJanice's Parcel\nProvided: Janice's Parcel","desc":"She's a tad ornery, and quite possibly out of her gourd... but the records indicate that Ol' Emma does fit the framework of who Emma Felstone might be.\nPerhaps you've seen Ol' Emma wander the city - she talks to herself, most often in nonsensical jibber-jabber. Still, she doesn't hurt anything or anyone, so folks pretty much leave her be.\nAll things considered, I would say that Ol' Emma is in fact Emma Felstone. You might try asking if her last name is indeed Felstone.","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I would tell you to get off my lawn, but as you can see I don't have one.","done":"My name is indeed Emma Felstone - you're the first person in years to call me that. Who... who are you?\nYou say you knew... my sister?! Is she still alive? Who am I kidding, of course she isn't. When the plague broke out in Lordaeron, I had come to expect the worst. So many of my family died... or worse. Here I am now, crazy Ol' Emma, all alone. What are you, a grave-robber or something? Looking for your next target?\nWhat... you have a package for me from my sister?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.2,"y":48.1,"n":"Royal Factor Bathrilor","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.2,"y":57,"n":"Ol' Emma","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"568":{"id":568,"t":"The Defense of Grom'gol","lv":36,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Aggro'gosh of the Grom'gol base camp wants you to kill 15 Lashtail Raptors.\nLashtail Raptor slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Throm'ka, ‹class›!\nYour arrival at Grom'gol is timely, indeed. As commander of the Warchief's base camp here in the jungle I am bound by honor to ensure the safety of all members of the Horde. Our mission to provide a safe chain of supply to Stonard is being hampered by some of the local inhabitants.\nI am putting you in charge of thinning out the raptor population outside of Grom'gol. Once you have made significant progress, report back to me for reassignment.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Our supply efforts are still being hampered by the indigenous raptor population, ‹class›.","done":"Your duty was performed with honor, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":28.9,"n":"Commander Aggro'gosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"328":{"id":328,"t":"The Hidden Key","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Small Brass Key to open Bookie Herod's Strongbox.\nSmall Brass Key\nProvided: Small Brass Key","desc":"Although no mention of Private Thorsen is found in these records, hidden within the binding of one of Herod's ledger books is a small, brass key.\nAnd after further study of his notes, a few references to a \"secure strongbox\" are contained among various papers. The box is somewhere within the Stockpile - the cavern complex at the back of Kurzen's Compound.\nIf this secure strongbox is found, and the small brass key can open it, then perhaps the mystery behind Thorsen's detection will be revealed.","rew":"You will receive:\nBookmaker's Scepter\nExperience: 1,400\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The strongbox is bound in bronze, very sturdy, and very heavy.","done":"Opening the strongbox, it's clear that this is where Herod keeps his more valuable coins and items.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":43.7,"y":9.4,"n":"Bookie Herod's Records","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":49.6,"y":7.6,"n":"Bookie Herod's Strongbox","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"97048":{"id":97048,"t":"Returning to port","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Captain Aransas in Booty Bay.","desc":"Listen, I can't repay you right now, but I'm a cook on Captain Aransas' ship. I'll be sure to put in a good word for you when I get back to Booty Bay. You should speak to the captain when you get the chance. I'm sure she'll be grateful to have me back.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKurzen Headshrinker's Cinch Jailer's Discarded Chain Crusty Cuffs\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\nLevel 38 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 34 36 41 48 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 97048","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5848":{"id":5848,"t":"Of Love and Family","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme, in the northern part of the Plaguelands. It is in the Scarlet Bastion that you will find the painting 'Of Love and Family,' hidden behind another painting depicting the twin moons of our world.\nReturn the painting to Tirion Fordring.\nOf Love and Family Unfinished Painting in Stratholme","desc":"The painting... It hung on the wall of my workshop - inside the Order's barracks - for years.\nAfter Tirion's trial was over, I knew that I could no longer keep the painting visible. I hid it in a place that they would never think to look.\nTravel to Stratholme and make your way deep inside what is now the Scarlet Bastion, search for a painting of our twin moons. Chip away at the paint until you uncover my master work, 'Of Love and Family.'\nMay the Light guide your actions.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"The painting, ‹name›. Do you have the painting?","done":"<Tirion nearly collapses when he sees the painting.>\n<He begins to sob in an almost frenetic manner.>\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":65.8,"y":75.4,"n":"Artist Renfray","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"8968":{"id":8968,"t":"The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth Jarien and Sothos and slay them. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLeft Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet Mor Grayhoof , Isalien , Jarien , Sothos and 1 more\nBrazier of Beckoning\nJarien slain\nSothos slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"The siblings, Jarien and Sothos, decided to join the Scarlet Crusade upon the disbanding of our mercenary company. They took the left piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet with them. Good riddance, I say, but we need that piece back.\nFrom what we could gather, they were actually slain by Grand Crusader Dathrohan himself for failing the initiation rites inside his chamber in the Scarlet Bastion.\nIn any case, we... meaning you, are still going to need to retrieve that piece of the amulet.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Does this mean then, ‹class›, that you've already put the souls of those two fools to rest and retrieved the left piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet?","done":"I suppose it's for the best that the souls of those two have finally been put to rest, even if I didn't like them while they were alive. In any case, we have what we were after, and that is definitely a good thing!\nUnfortunately, I do not know the location of the one who died with the right piece of the amulet in their possession. But do not fear; in life I was a dabbler in the art of divination, so I have another task for you, which is going to enable us to ferret out the final piece.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"3528":{"id":3528,"t":"The God Hakkar","lv":53,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Egg of Hakkar to Yeh'kinya in Tanaris.\nFilled Egg of Hakkar\nProvided: Egg of Hakkar","desc":"Now it is time to capture the essence of the avatar of Hakkar.\nTake the Egg of Hakkar to the Sanctum of the Fallen God in the Sunken Temple in Azeroth. Invoke the egg's power to stir the dead god.\nHe will send his minions against you. Defeat his bloodrinkers and take their Hakkari blood, then use the blood to dowse the eternal flames that hold Hakkar's spirit. When all the flames go out, the avatar of Hakkar will enter our world.\nDefeat him, and place his essence within the egg of Hakkar.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAvenguard Helm Lifeforce Dirk Gemburst Circlet\nMoney: 2 40 2 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,900","back":"Have you defeated the avatar of Hakkar, ‹name›? Has his essence yet empowered the egg I gave you?","done":"The essence of Hakkar has been collected! Even now the Egg stirs with life! Could the myths of Hakkar be true?\nThat must not be true, for it is then I fear what Hakkar may do if birthed again. I will keep this egg safe and be sure it does not fall into evil hands.\nYour labors with me are finished, ‹name›. You have touched a legend, and your actions may one day change the face of our world.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67,"y":22.4,"n":"Yeh'kinya","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"648":{"id":648,"t":"Rescue OOX-17/TN!","lv":48,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort OOX-17/TN to Steamwheedle Port, then report to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.","desc":"The gnome's voice crackles once again from the robot:\n\"I need to move OOX-17/TN to an open, safe place so it can begin a lengthy take-off procedure. It has built-in cloaking, but I need time on my end to make it operational again. I need you to escort the robot from its current location to, let's say, Steamwheedle Port! That should be a perfect place, and long enough, to get things on line!\"\n\"Escort it safely to the port, and then come talk to me in Booty Bay! Oglethorpe Obnoticus - out!\"","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOptomatic Deflector Thermotastic Egg Timer\nExperience: 5,450\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"Oh, YOU'RE the great savior of OOX-17/TN! I cannot even begin to express my thanks for your assistance! My homing robot series needs more developing, but your recovery has saved me countless hours of rebuilding time, as well as many gold pieces in rebinding costs!\nPlease, take your choice of any of these items I have. Hopefully, you will make good use of one of them. Thank you again for your generous assistance, my robots and I are in your debt!\nTanaris Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":60.2,"y":64.7,"n":"Homing Robot OOX-17/TN","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8728":{"id":8728,"t":"The Good News and The Bad News","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris wants you to bring him 20 Arcanite Bars, 10 Elementium Ore, 10 Azerothian Diamonds, and 10 Blue Sapphires.\n20 Arcanite Bar\n10 Elementium Ore Blackwing Technician 7.7 % in Blackwing Lair\n10 Azerothian Diamond Hakkari Thorium Vein 1.2 % , Large Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Thorium Vein 0.7 % and 4 more\n10 Blue Sapphire Alzzin's Minion 2.5 % , Rich Thorium Vein 0.8 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 0.8 % , Small Thorium Vein 0.7 % and 4 more","desc":"Well that took a little longer than expected. Now let me see what this ledger says.\n<Narain silently reads the ledger, periodically mumbling under his breath.>\nThe good news is that I am 99% certain that I am capable of creating an arcanite buoy that will function to your specifications. This is, of course, wholly dependant on the bad news.\nThe bad news is that I'm going to need a lot of arcanite, elementium ore, and rare gemstones.\nBring me what I need and I will craft the buoy.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Arcanite buoys don't just make themselves, ‹name›. And NO, you cannot borrow some money.","done":"A deal is a deal. I sure hope you know what you are getting yourself into, ‹name›. This is an awful lot of trouble to go through to do some fishing.\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"488":{"id":488,"t":"Zenn's Bidding","lv":5,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Zenn Foulhoof outside of Dolanaar 3 Nightsaber Fangs, 3 Strigid Owl Feathers and 3 swatches of Webwood Spider Silk.\n3 Nightsaber Fang Elder Nightsaber 21 % , Feral Nightsaber 21 % , Nightsaber 21 % , Nightsaber Stalker 21 % and 1 more\n3 Strigid Owl Feather Strigid Owl 35 % , Strigid Screecher 35 % , Strigid Hunter 35 %\n3 Webwood Spider Silk Webwood Lurker 27 % , Webwood Venomfang 27 % , Webwood Silkspinner 27 % , Giant Webwood Spider 27 %","desc":"Eager for work, I see. Lucky for you a day never goes by that I don't wish I had a fledgling ‹class› to perform my bidding.\nYou see, ‹name›, I can make you very happy and provide you with things you never dreamed of having. But in order for that to happen you must bring me certain items.\nMy business in the forest often requires certain. . .reagents. Fetch for me 3 Nightsaber Fangs, 3 Strigid Owl Feathers and 3 swatches of Webwood Spider Silk.\nLet's keep this our little secret, ‹race›.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Severed Voodoo Claw\nMoney: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 450","back":"Have you been a busy little bee, ‹name›? I've been waiting for you to bring me what I need.","done":"Ha ha! Well, done indeed.\nWho would have ever guessed that I, Zenn Foulhoof, would have a ‹race› to do my bidding? Certainly not me! But so it goes... this beloved world of ours is full of surprises.\nThree cheers for the naive and gullible!","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.5,"y":56.3,"n":"Zenn Foulhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"87288":{"id":87288,"t":"Soft saber pelts","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 6 Soft Nightsaber Pelts to Aldria.\n6 Soft Nightsaber Pelt","desc":"Hello, traveler! I hope you are enjoying your visit to our village. I like Dolanaar because it is small and rustic and everyone is friendly.\nI'm a local trader, and I bring in all sorts of tools and trinkets that might be useful to you in your travels. Indeed, if you are interested in a trade, I find myself in need of some nightsaber pelts. While these majestic creatures are beautiful, the local ones are rather aggressive, so don't feel too bad about defending yourself.","rew":"You will receive:\nSoft Saber Sack\nExperience: 625\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"It is good to see you again! Are you here to trade?","done":"Oh, these are wonderful. It is a shame to resort to violence with such majestic animals, but it is important to keep the roads safe, and these pelts will make beautiful blankets and shawls.\nHere, let me give you something to remember them. It is both soft and sturdy.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":57.2,"n":"Aldia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"888":{"id":888,"t":"Stolen Booty","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Shipment of Boots and Telescopic Lens for Gazlowe in Ratchet.\nShipment of Boots Drizzlik's Emporium\nTelescopic Lens Fragile - Do Not Drop","desc":"While I'd like to recover all my goods, I'm sure that's not possible. Still, there's a few things that I absolutely must have!\nAs you see, my observatory is ready to go, but it needs the smaller of the two lenses. The first arrived by caravan from Durotar, but the second was bound by ship, and never arrived. Also, I never got my boot shipment from Drizzlik in Booty Bay!\nHead down to the pirate camp and see if you can find them.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWayfaring Gloves Padded Lamellar Boots\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Did you find my things, ‹name›?","done":"It's a relief to get all this stuff back, so thanks for your help, ‹name›. You know, I could use a ‹race› like you to help out with my operation here. If you're ever looking for work, don't forget about how well Gazlowe pays for service!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"168":{"id":168,"t":"Collecting Memories","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Worn Miner's Waistcord. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Retrieve 4 Miners' Union Cards and return them to Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind.\n4 Miners' Union Card Undead Dynamiter , Undead Excavator , Skeletal Miner","desc":"Many of my friends perished that horrible day when the mine tunnel caved in. If your adventures happen to bring you into that wing of the mine in Moonbrook, please keep an eye out for any sign which might identify them. If you come across any of their Miners' Union Cards, bring them back to me and I'll make sure their families get some resolution from this horrible accident.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTunneler's Boots Dusty Mining Gloves Worn Miner's Waistcord\nNew in Forever: Worn Miner's Waistcord.\nExperience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Were you able to retrieve any of my old co-worker's Miners' Union Cards?","done":"Thank you for collecting these, ‹name›. Your efforts will help bring peace to the dead in the wake of this tragedy. I will see to it that the families are notified.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":70.3,"y":40.8,"n":"Wilder Thistlenettle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-deadmines"]},"2968":{"id":2968,"t":"A Future Task","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Sage Truthseeker in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Well ‹name›... we seem to be at an unfortunate impasse. We know what we need - the Plates of Uldum - but we have no idea where they might be. We will research this, and then devise a solid plan of attack. I have a couple ideas where to start looking; I have high hopes that soon, we'll be asking you to rejoin our efforts to discover the truth.\nSage Truthseeker needs to be informed on this, ‹name›; no doubt, he also wants to thank you personally for once again heeding the call.","rew":"Money: 2 20 2 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"We're all in agreement then - the best course of action is to wait until we can narrow down the areas where these plates might lie hidden. You've brought us this far ‹name›, and I hope you will be the one to head back in to the field to confront the secrets of Uldum.\nAllow me to give you this honorarium in the meantime; this should cover any expenses you've encountered in assisting us, and a little something extra. Be sure to check back with us soon... Uldum beckons us all, young one.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":34.4,"y":46.9,"n":"Sage Truthseeker","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"8":{"id":8,"t":"A Rogue's Deal","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Nondescript Letter to Innkeeper Renee in Tirisfal Glades.\nNondescript Letter\nProvided: Nondescript Letter","desc":"Hey, mate! Do a favor for a young man who's been fighting more than his fair share of mindless zombies and spiders?\nI got this here letter that needs to go to Brill... to an innkeeper named Renee something-or-other. Don't really matter none what her last name is.\nAnyway, it's a nice cozy little place full of victims of the plague trying to make their way in the world. And it be a great spot for you to rest too if the need arises. You should check it out... you do and I'll pay you well.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Forest Mushroom Cap 5 Refreshing Spring Water\nExperience: 110\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes? Yes? What is it?\nThe forsaken; they certainly do have huge appetites. Make yourself at home... yes, rest those weary bones. My name's Renee if you need anything at all.","done":"Oh? A letter? Wonderful news! I've been waiting on word from my dear old mother in Deathknell. Such a saint, she is. I wonder how she's holding up.\nWhat? Too cheery? Not buying it, are you?\nWell, get lost then... it's really no business who the letter's from anyway. Go on! Get lost!\nCome back when you've got some coin to spend... loafer.\nNext thing you know, you'll be coming back to rest after a long days adventure or some stupid thing like that.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":38.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Calvin Montague","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":52,"n":"Innkeeper Renee","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"408":{"id":408,"t":"The Family Crypt","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Wailing Ancestors and 8 Rotting Ancestors.\nKill Captain Dargol, and bring his skull to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.\nDargol's Skull Captain Dargol\nWailing Ancestor slain : 0/ 8\nRotting Ancestor slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The Agamand Mills area has become a foothold for the Scourge. Their strongest point is the Agamand Family Crypt where their local military leader, a skeleton named Captain Dargol, has headquartered. With Necromancy he has raised the ancestors of the Agamands and plans to use them against us.\nThis cannot pass, and you must stop it. Travel to the Agamand Family Crypt and defeat the raised Agamand ancestors.\nAnd, bring me the skull of Captain Dargol.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDarkwood Staff Bonecracker\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Time is not a luxury we have, ‹name›. With each passing hour, the Scourge's hold on Tirisfal Glades grows more firm.","done":"Your actions struck a telling blow against the Scourge. And your victory will not go unnoticed - not by the Forsaken, nor by our enemies.\nContinue the struggle as we all do, ‹name›, and one day we will drive the Lich King himself from Azeroth!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"1688":{"id":1688,"t":"Surena Caledon","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Surena's Choker for Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.\nSurena's Choker Surena Caledon","desc":"I had a student named Surena Caledon. She stood where you stand now, eager to learn of warlock magic, and possessing no small bit of talent. More than that she was young and pleasing to the eye. Had I seen it then, the traitorous trollop!\nThe thieving wench ran off with one of the Defias, Erlan Drudgemoor. While her loss is of little importance, I gifted her a bloodstone choker that I must have.\nHer life means nothing to me now. You will find her at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. Retrieve what is mine.","rew":"Experience: 625","back":"Even the older and wiser can be unmanned by the wiles of youth and beauty, ‹name›. A piece of advice you would do well to remember throughout your life.","done":"Surena was talented, but not enough so to gain mastery of warlock magic on her own. It's a shame to see talent wasted, but sometimes it is necessary.\nI hope my investment in you will bear different results.\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4968":{"id":4968,"t":"Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Hmm, you've made it this far... truly astonishing. I would have thought the corruption of channeling the arcane would have seeped into your very soul and driven you mad by now. How about we try and push you further then?\nIf you want to test your skill, seek out Menara Voidrender above Ratchet in Strahad's tower. She will guide you.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"Ah, you do seek something more... substantial. That I can help you if you truly are prepared.\nIt's a welcome change to see one of our kind seeking more power in forms other than just knowledge.\nSo, do you feel you're ready, ‹name›?\nStormwind City The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85,"n":"Demisette Cloyce","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4488":{"id":4488,"t":"Summon Felsteed","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.","desc":"Ah, ‹name›, you've seen fit to grace us with your presence. How wonderful!\nI hope you do not expect us to wait on you hand and foot also. You may be growing quickly in power, but you still are a pup when it comes to true knowledge and understanding. If you're not careful, corruption will overwhelm you and your weak will.\nBut I should get to the point: Strahad wishes to speak to you. He is still residing in his tower overlooking Ratchet in the Barrens. I suggest not taking too long.\nStormwind City The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85,"n":"Demisette Cloyce","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1848":{"id":1848,"t":"Brutal Hauberk","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nBrutal Hauberk\nExperience: 3,050","done":"I am sure you endured much hardship and shed much blood on my task, ‹name›. Here is the product of your toil.\nMay you wear it well, and may you one day return here with stories of its service to you.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8568":{"id":8568,"t":"Past Victories in Warsong Gulch","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Warsong Mark of Honor","desc":"Ah, yes! Of course we wouldn't forget about your past accomplishments in Warsong Gulch.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 8568","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8408":{"id":8408,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! You've served the Alliance well.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"93928":{"id":93928,"t":"Of mice and milk","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Get the mouse a cookie.","desc":"I need a cookie, see?\nNyeah!","done":"(PH) Thanks!\nWestfall Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":52.8,"y":54.2,"n":"Mouse","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"5128":{"id":5128,"t":"Words of the High Chief","lv":59,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Crudely-written Log to Kelek Skykeeper in southern Felwood.\nCrudely-written Log High Chief Winterfall\nProvided: Crudely-written Log","desc":"The Winterfall are no longer a threat to me, but if you still want to find out what was driving the furbolg to create and consume this strange firewater, I think you should seek out Kelek Skykeeper.\nHe is part of a group known as the Emerald Circle, druids that are committed to their work in Felwood, healing the land from the corruption.\nKelek has much experience with the furbolgs in Felwood, and may be able to tell you more about the log.\nThank you, again, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Everlook","back":"The Emerald Circle is friendly to all, ‹race›. What can I do for you?","done":"Yes, if you let me examine this for a while, I might be able to translate it for you.\n<Kelek flips through the pages.>\nWhen I am able to look over this fully, I will send word to you.\nThank you for sharing this with me, ‹name›. Very little is known about the Winterfall furbolg.\nWinterspring Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":51.1,"y":81.8,"n":"Kelek Skykeeper","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"94568":{"id":94568,"t":"The cults true plans","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong and observe the conversation.\nLearn what you can from the crystal\nObserve the conversation","desc":"The turncoat clearly was afraid of the what the cult had planned, enough so to defect and seek our aid. It's truly unfortunate that he is dead and took his secrets to the grave with him.\nWe must discuss this further to determine our next steps.","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"That turncoat risked everything to escape the cult and bring us this crystal...","done":"We could try and send peacekeepers to directly engage the cult forces, but we would not fare well against them in open battle.\nWe are going to need a different approach.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94488":{"id":94488,"t":"The ties that bind","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill Commander Haalien and bring his head to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.\nCommander Haalien's Severed Head","desc":"The reason for cultists presence here still baffles me, but I smell a familiar scent over the bloodshed.\nOne of our circle druids, Haalien, disappeared months back. It appears he's thrown his sorry hide in with the cultists.\nShow him what happens when he spills the blood of his kin! Take his head and return it to me.","back":"Are our brethren's lives truly worth so little to you, Haalien?","done":"<Elegael grimaces at the severed head, but nods curtly.>\nThank you, Thaildras. No matter how much rage I have within me, it would have been difficult to strike down my own cousin.\nDo not mourn for him. His ignorance and malice has killed many innocents this day.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"9208":{"id":9208,"t":"The Savage Guard - Arcanum of Protection","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Zanza the Restless in Zul'Gurub wants an Arcanum of Protection.\nArcanum of Protection","desc":"Zanza can create many ancient troll enchantments with proper components! Have you heard of the Savage Guard? No, of course you haven't. Your mind is addled with the inferior elven magic.\nBring me an arcanum of elven creation so that I may destroy the aberration. Do this and the Savage Guard will be yours.","rew":"You will receive:\nSavage Guard\n+200 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Do you have the arcanum?","done":"The worthless magic in these enchantments fuels my anger. My anger gives me strength.\nBring me more and you shall receive another Savage Guard.\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 9208","cats":["zulgurub"]}});